// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: static `SLOT` may not be a reference
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: `&Int` is a reference
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: declare a `borrows` accessor
//
// The no-escape position matrix, row "static declaration" (design 193 unit 5).
// A static is the longest-lived storage in the language — it outlives every
// call in the program — so it is the position the rule most obviously covers,
// and it was the one nothing checked. Before this it fell out as two errors
// about OTHER things (an initializer type mismatch, and a Sync complaint about
// `&Int`), neither of which says what is actually wrong with the declaration.

static SLOT: &Int = 0

func main() {
    print("unreachable")
}
